{
  "id": "ss.relic.oxygen",
  "name": "Swollen spiracle",
  "description": "A pair of lungs packed past what they hold, and the air already coming off them: two dark blue-grey lobes either side of a pale windpipe, each with a bright cyan core showing through as though the organ were lit from inside, and three beads climbing away off one shoulder. The first pass drew the spiracle itself — a chitin ring around a dark throat — and it read as an orange eye and nothing else, so the ring is gone. The beads escape on a diagonal rather than flanking the windpipe evenly: set symmetrically they became a second pair of eyes above the first, which is the same failure the ring had. The cyan is the only saturated colour here and it is the substance the relic is named for; the vessel around it stays desaturated so the two never compete.",
